# A formal cannot satisfy a missing DATA receiver requirement; no body or RHS runs.
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the record is `call(args := Args; code := D\Code)` (the former `call(Args D Code)` is no form). The
# inputs of the launch are described by the data parent(Code) = D, which declares seen; x is a declaration of the code
# of Code, not an input of D. The field x of Args names no input: 5, before its value is read; no body or RHS runs
# (Observed\before 1, Observed\after 0, calls 0, D\seen 0).
# Norm: the book #structural-call («The input places, requirements and defaults are described by the data parent(C)»),
# #declaration-selection (a named actual that names no input admits no form).
Observed:
    int: before 0
    int: after 0
    int: calls 0
end: Observed
int: calls 0
fn: side () int
    calls := calls + 1
    return: 2
Args:
    int: x 7
end: Args
D:
    int: seen 0
    Code:
        seen := 1
        int: x side()
    end: Code
end: D
Main:
    Observed\before := 1
    call(args := Args; code := D\Code)
    Observed\after := 1
    Observed\calls := calls
